  "prefLabel": "Puc 402.13 Payphone",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Puc 402.13 \"Payphone\" means any telephone made available to the public on a fee-per-call basis, independent of any other commercial transaction, for the purpose of making telephone calls, whether the telephone is activated by depositing coins, by calling collect, or by using a credit card.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note # 1, Revision Note #2, and Revision Note #3 at chapter heading for Puc 400) #14029, eff 7-25-24",
